    dict(key='18-act-4-figure', kind='figure', title='A waiver that ends',
         body='waiver_timeline',
         narration="Fourth demo: exceptions. [[slnc 400]] The agent really needs the host network, so the finding is waived. [[slnc 300]] A waiver here has a rule, a resource, an owner, a reason, and an end date. [[slnc 700]] On the timeline, the green bar is the waiver's life: it ends on the thirty first of December, twenty twenty six. [[slnc 300]] On the twenty second of October, it hides the finding: zero left. [[slnc 300]] On the first of January, twenty twenty seven, it has ended. [[slnc 300]] The finding comes back, and the waiver is reported as stale. [[slnc 600]] Below, two waivers that hide nothing. [[slnc 300]] One has no owner, and one names another resource. [[slnc 300]] An exception without an owner and an end date is not an exception. It is a hole."),
    dict(key='19-act-4-1', kind='console', title='Act Four — Exceptions: a waiver with an owner and an end',
         body='FOUR. Exceptions: a waiver with an owner and an end.\n  THE FINDING (fixed files):\n    K6   DaemonSet/metrics-agent agent\n  THE WAIVER:\n    for     K6 on DaemonSet/metrics-agent\n    owner   platform team\n    reason  reads node counters from the host network\n    ends    2026-12-31\n  THE RESULT (findings left, by day and waiver):\n    2026-10-22  this waiver          0\n    2027-01-01  this waiver          1, and 1 stale waiver\n    2026-10-22  no owner             1\n    2026-10-22  another resource     1',
         narration='The input: the one finding left, and a waiver for it, owned by the platform team, ending on the thirty first of December. [[slnc 400]] The result: zero findings before the end, one after, and the waiver is stale. [[slnc 300]] No owner, or another resource: the waiver hides nothing.'),
    dict(key='20-act-4-2', kind='console', title='Act Four — Exceptions: a waiver with an owner and an end',
         body='FOUR. (continued)\n  THE SAME INSIDE THE TOOLS:\n    checkov  annotation checkov.io/skip1: CKV_K8S_19\n    trivy    .trivyignore with the line KSV-0009\n  THE RESULT (does the host network check still fail?):\n    CKV_K8S_19  before yes   after no\n    KSV-0009    before yes   after no',
         narration='The same inside the tools: an annotation for Checkov, and an ignore file for Trivy. [[slnc 300]] Both checks stop failing. [[slnc 300]] But neither has an owner or an end date.'),
